ual columns and payment icons.\n\nRather than inventing a fake phone number, I'll keep things safer by using email addresses like sales@yogadirect.com and support@yogadirect.com, with a note about fast reply times. Now I'm ready to write out the full page, including a 10-14 item improvements list and the navigation links across index, shop, wholesale, and product pages.\n\nI'm drafting the index.html content: a promo bar about free shipping and wholesale savings, a nav with Yoga Mats, Props, Studio Packs, Wholesale, and About links plus Help and Cart, and a hero section emphasizing factory-direct pricing and studio-grade quality since 1999.\n\nNow I'm adding CTAs for shopping best sellers and wholesale pricing, trust-building ticks about shipping speed and bulk discounts, floating review cards, a trust bar with stats on years in business and mats shipped, and starting a shop-by-category section with pricing for mats and blocks.\n\nContinuing with more categories like wedges, straps, bolsters, blankets, and studio packs, then best sellers with add-to-cart buttons, a bulk pricing tier table with discount percentages, a quote CTA, why-us section, reviews, newsletter signup offering 10% off, FAQ, footer, and the drawer script. Now I'm starting the shop.html page with its header, breadcrumb, and heading for shopping mats and props.\n\nI'm planning out the shop page's filter chips, twelve product cards, bulk banner, and small FAQ, then moving to the product detail page for the pro-grip mat with its gallery, pricing, quantity selector, bulk pricing table, bundle upsell checkboxes, specs, and sticky mobile bar. I'm also sketching the wholesale page with its lead capture form and tiers, and the about page covering the company's history since 1999, manufacturing, and sustainability story.\n\nNow I'm outlining the contact page with its options, form, FAQ links, and hours, then planning to write one shared CSS file to paste across all six pages, defining the section, grid, card