il popup after a delay, an accordion, a quantity selector, and a sticky bar.\n\nWriting shared CSS...\n\nNow I'm sketching the home page HTML structure, thinking about adding Product schema markup and review snippets for SEO along with proper meta tags. For the placeholder product images, I'm planning a reusable class with several gradient variants paired with a centered SVG glyph to keep things visually distinct, then moving into drafting the home page sections starting with an announcement bar about free shipping and bulk pricing.\n\nI'm laying out the full page flow: header, hero, trust strip, categories, best sellers, a bundle offer band, wholesale CTA, why-us section, reviews, newsletter, FAQ, and footer, making sure nav links stay consistent across pages like shop, product, wholesale, and about.\n\nNow I need to output everything as valid JSON, so I'm writing the HTML content as single long lines with spaces instead of newlines to avoid any escaping issues, then drafting each page's markup this way.\n\nWriting shared CSS styles...\n\nAdding button and header styles...\n\nFor the product placeholders, I'll use a simple concentric-circle SVG icon resembling a rolled mat end view, varying the gradient colors per product to keep things visually distinct without much effort. Then I'll finalize everything, including generic but believable customer testimonials for the reviews section.\n\nNow I'm setting up volume pricing tiers for the product page with discounts scaling from 10% to 30% off based on quantity, plus JavaScript to update the displayed unit price and total dynamically. I'm also writing cart logic that tracks item count in localStorage, updates the cart badge across the page, and shows a toast notification, along with an email capture modal triggered by a timer or exit intent using sessionStorage to avoid repeat popups, and a FAQ accordion built with native details elements.\n\nNow I'm building the shared header markup, including an announcement bar about